Description: Expose the r7 S Pen tablet/touch toggle in phosh-mobile-settings
 Three parts:
 (1) debian/rules: set tweaks-data-dir to /usr/share/phosh-mobile-settings/tweaks
     (Droidian's default is ''), so that tweaks/spen.yaml shipped by the adaptation
     package - the org.droidian.spen finger-mode toggle - shows up in Settings.
     .nobuiltins.desktop added to .install for dh_missing.
 (2) An optional "icon" property for Configurable Tweaks pages, completing
     upstream's "TODO: Read icon from ... settings definitions" note: page->icon
     is added to the parser, and ms-window.c uses the page's own icon instead of
     the fixed "conf-tweaks-symbolic". The S Pen page gets input-tablet-symbolic.
 Built on top of droidian group/next/phosh-0.55 (commit 3fbecf5). Must be built on
 the device - libcellbroadcast-dev is not installable in the build container.
Author: Yunus Tan <yunus.tan@outlook.com.tr>
Origin: downstream, r7 (SM-N770F) Droidian port
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-07-26
---
diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index ad7a43c..bbe3889 100644
--- a/debian/changelog
+++ b/debian/changelog
@@ -1,3 +1,12 @@
+phosh-mobile-settings (0.55.0+git20260527214851.3fbecf5.next.phosh.0.55+r7spen1) experimental; urgency=medium
+
+  * r7 (SM-N770F): set tweaks-data-dir to /usr/share/phosh-mobile-settings/tweaks
+    (Droidian's default was empty), so that the S Pen tablet/touch toggle
+    (Configurable Tweaks / tweaks/spen.yaml, org.droidian.spen finger-mode)
+    appears in Settings.
+
+ -- Yunus Tan <yunus.tan@outlook.com.tr>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:49:30 +0300
+
 phosh-mobile-settings (0.55.0) experimental; urgency=medium
 
   [ nicole mikołajczyk ]
